  "id": "Compound::DB01102 - Gene::155",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests that Arbutamine may interact with Adrb3 through a series of molecular relationships involving beta-adrenergic agonists and organic amino compounds. Path_12470 indicates that Arbutamine binds to Adrb1, which is then bound by Fenoterol, and Fenoterol binds to Adrb3. This pathway links Arbutamine to Adrb3 via a chain of receptor interactions, with the lowest common ancestor of Arbutamine and Fenoterol being a beta-adrenergic agonist. Path_12471 and Path_12472 further support this by showing that Arbutamine resembles Dobutamine and Masoprocol, both of which are beta-adrenergic agonists, and that these compounds bind to Adrb3. The shared ancestry of Arbutamine with these compounds, along with the binding of Fenoterol to Adrb3, suggests a potential mechanism by which Arbutamine may influence Adrb3 activity. The evidence is consistent with a role for beta-adrenergic receptors in the interaction between Arbutamine and Adrb3, though the exact nature of the interaction remains uncertain due to the limited direct evidence provided.",
